  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1138 PM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nDry weather and a gradual warming trend are expected late this\nweekend through much of next week as ridging becomes established.\nTemperatures will be near normal to just above normal through the\nperiod. A trough over the northern Great Plains may send a\nbackdoor front southward into eastern NM around Tuesday \nnight/Wednesday, although there are still model differences and \nuncertainty regarding the timing and extent of the boundary. Any \ncooling looks to be modest and precipitation limited.\n\nBy the end of next week, long-term guidance hints at a Pacific\nsystem potentially moving inland. Unsettled weather may be in \nstore, but details will need to be refined in future forecasts as \nthis is over a week away.",
